  "the-high-priestess": "something known and not yet said out loud",
  "the-empress": "something growing that needs feeding, not starting",
  "the-hierophant": "the proper way of doing it, and what it costs to belong",
  "the-chariot": "already moving, and it goes where you point it",
  "strength": "holding something strong by hand, gently, every day",
  "the-hermit": "gone up alone on purpose, and holding the light",
  "wheel-of-fortune": "a change that comes from outside and does not ask",
  "justice": "what was actually done, weighed and answered for",
  "the-hanged-man": "a wait you agreed to, paid for in time",
  "death": "an ending already decided, coming at walking pace",
  "temperance": "two things becoming one, at the speed of a season",
